{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/781829-statting-up-a-ts-ritual-for-illness-transfer","id":781829,"title":"Statting up a TS ritual for illness transfer.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-07T13:53:22-08:00","id":781829,"title":"Statting up a TS ritual for illness transfer.","content":"Simple concept: There has been references to theban sorcery rite that allows the Kindred to be purified of illness. I don't think this has been stated up before but the concept that I have for it is the Vampire shifts the illness that she is currently suffering from onto a mortal (who deals it normally). Fluff is that the rite is more of a shame on the offending Kindred (as &quot;only disease afflicts those who stray from their duties&quot;) while held as a boon to the mortal which given weird LS logic, is closer to knowing God's workers are among it and by helping them out and maybe dying, they will ascend to the heavens. Hence targeting people who are most likely already suffering terminal illnesses and sending them on their way a wee bit faster.<br /> <br /> Only issue is working out the offering and the dot level. Given the rarity, I'm mostly thinking 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T18:06:54-08:00","id":781985,"title":"","content":"I agree for the 4th dot. Since Kindred carry disease and illness in the blood and the ritual seems to purify the blood of the Kindred and pass it on to someone else, it might require some kind of pure, untainted blood in a vessel. Maybe virginal? Or perhaps youthful? (Like a small amount of blood from a young child, since they've never experienced serious illness theoretically.) Admittedly, those are a bit edgy. Maybe a sample of untainted blood from a sick person? (The target, no less.) That's certainly not as easy to get, especially if they've been sick for years. It might then make it an incentive for the Sanctified to target people who are recently ill. Like you ever heard a story about someone who just took ill and it just gets way worse way quickly and they're dead? It might look like that in many cases, that way it reinforces a sort of tragic narrative. Young people or the healthy who are &quot;too good for this world&quot; and all that.<br /> <br /> Some ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:20:25-08:00","id":782290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/781829-statting-up-a-ts-ritual-for-illness-transfer?p=781985#post781985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree for the 4th dot. Since Kindred carry disease and illness in the blood and the ritual seems to purify the blood of the Kindred and pass it on to someone else, it might require some kind of pure, untainted blood in a vessel. Maybe virginal? Or perhaps youthful? (Like a small amount of blood from a young child, since they've never experienced serious illness theoretically.) Admittedly, those are a bit edgy. Maybe a sample of untainted blood from a sick person? (The target, no less.) That's certainly not as easy to get, especially if they've been sick for years. It might then make it an incentive for the Sanctified to target people who are recently ill. Like you ever heard a story about someone who just took ill and it just gets way worse way quickly and they're dead? It might look like that in many cases, that way it reinforces a sort of tragic narrative. Young people or the healthy who are &quot;too good for this world&quot; and all that.<br /> <br /> Some ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work but blood offerings tend to be more of Cr\u00faac's domain than TB.<br /> <br /> After doing a bit of research, I am seeing another option towards using the fangs of an egyptian asp. Reasons being is snake symbols are heavily involved in medicine and there is the story of the Nehushtan in the bible which incorporates such animals as punishment for straying. It also hints back at the idea of TB steals a bit from egyptian mystics which has been a ongoing thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}